# MyFileExplorer agent rules

## Scope

- This repo is **MyFileExplorer** — a standalone Windows file manager (Electron + React).
- **Do not** reference, import, copy from, or depend on any other project (including any LoRA / training apps).
- Canonical plan: `PLAN.md`. Specs: `docs/`. Implement against those files only.

## Architecture

- Electron main owns filesystem, shell, session, settings, preview parse, search index, thumbs.
- Renderer is React + Zustand; **no Node integration**.
- Typed preload IPC + Zod; Result envelope `{ ok, value } | { ok: false, error }`.
- App state only under Electron `userData` — never write app sidecars into arbitrary browsed folders.

## Safety

- Validate/normalize all paths in main before IO.
- Custom media protocol is allowlisted only.
- Del → Recycle Bin; Shift+Del permanent with confirms for multi/dir.
- Do not browse or exfiltrate user home/disk “to verify” beyond what the user asked.
- **HARD RULE:** the live `settings.json` (userData / `.dev-user-data`) is private. Never Read, Grep, or otherwise load it into the model. Local repo scripts may touch it on disk; do not bring the file body (or a dump of it) into chat. See [settings-privacy.mdc](settings-privacy.mdc).

## Specs vs code

Until scaffold exists, prefer updating `docs/` + `PLAN.md` when product decisions change; then implement.
Keep [docs/DECISIONS.md](docs/DECISIONS.md) in sync when locking behavior.

## Unpublished (developer gate)

- **Compiled file lists** is a private feature (D39). Keep every UI entry and IPC channel behind `devGateActive` / `isDevGateActive()`. Never mention it in README, CHANGELOG, RELEASE_NOTES, or `docs/` pages that users or GitHub issues will read. Do not add how-to docs or accept it as a public product request.
- Appearance **Show DEV-gated items** is visible only when `userData/DEV.cfg` exists. It writes `ENABLE` in that file. Do not create the file. Gated chrome still requires `ENABLE=true` **and** `COMPUTER_NAME` matching this machine. Do not document `DEV.cfg` in user-facing docs.

## Settings (D45)

- **Every new preference** must be added to `settingsSchema` (or a nested Zod object already under it) so Settings → Export / Import round-trips it automatically.
- Do not invent a parallel export allowlist. Only dialog/window geometry is stripped (`settingsExport.ts` `WINDOW_LIKE_KEYS`).
- Add/adjust a unit test in `src/tests/settingsExport.test.ts` when introducing non-obvious nested prefs.
